                                "text": "Outside the rand or steep edge of this dome the bog is permanently ringed around by a zone liable to base-rich flooding, and this zone, the lagg, carries a persistent fen or carr vegetation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2aaa46c-8926-4e2f-9dd3-c11268e4b8d4",
                                "sense_id": "0278e88d-5ae3-3093-ac55-fd9976ac16df",
                                "text": "Lagg (1) Marginal zone outside the rand containing fen vegetation and representing the transition between raised bog peat and mineral soils."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb21d8ba-60e6-47ac-a16e-88cc2846f471",
                                "sense_id": "0278e88d-5ae3-3093-ac55-fd9976ac16df",
                                "text": "[…] the rands, especially near the Teifi river, are very steep."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8e90c824-3d2e-3e01-ab9a-98a8f531c02e",
                        "entry_id": "e12c3984-e67d-3832-97c2-d59cf3dc41ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A strip of meat; a long fleshy piece of beef, cut from the flank or leg; a sort of steak."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dialectal",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "96ac7121-ba49-424e-b6c1-4e5406e31f25",
                                "sense_id": "8e90c824-3d2e-3e01-ab9a-98a8f531c02e",
                                "text": "They came with chopping-knives / To cut me into rands and sirloins"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6855d3a4-41b4-3b87-ad78-3fe26fb53182",
                        "entry_id": "e12c3984-e67d-3832-97c2-d59cf3dc41ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A border, edge or rim; a strip, as of cloth."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "dialectal",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce93fe6a-a505-49bf-aaed-a461f9a8fc9f",
                                "sense_id": "6855d3a4-41b4-3b87-ad78-3fe26fb53182",
                                "text": "They quarrelled an' fought 'mang the clippin's an' rands, / The tailor insistin' the colour was blue."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "55240e6c-e09c-37b7-b930-61d4fa09f038",
                        "entry_id": "e12c3984-e67d-3832-97c2-d59cf3dc41ed",
